===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|fakan|faką|piece, part|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|pāǵe-|to nail, fasten|lang=ang}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|fek|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon [[fak]] (Dutch [[vak]]), Old High German [[fah]] (German [[Fach]]), Latin [[pangere]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fæk/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=n|pl=facu}}

# a [[division]]
# an [[interval]], a portion, period, or space of time, while
# period of five years, [[lustrum]]

